<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Tech Genius | Deep Work Environment</title>

<style>
:root{
    --bg:#07111f;
    --bg2:#0b1728;
    --panel:#101f33;
    --panel2:#13263d;
    --line:#263c56;
    --text:#edf4fb;
    --muted:#9fb0c3;
    --accent:#58d6c0;
    --accent2:#8fa8ff;
    --warning:#e6c46a;
    --danger:#e98787;
    --white:#ffffff;
}

*{
    margin:0;
    padding:0;
    box-sizing:border-box;
}

html{
    scroll-behavior:smooth;
}

body{
    font-family:Inter,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",sans-serif;
    background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 20% 0%,rgba(88,214,192,.08),transparent 30%),
        radial-gradient(circle at 85% 15%,rgba(143,168,255,.08),transparent 30%),
        var(--bg);
    color:var(--text);
    line-height:1.65;
}

button,
input,
select,
textarea{
    font:inherit;
}

button{
    cursor:pointer;
}

/* =========================
   HERO
========================= */

.hero{
    min-height:600px;
    display:flex;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    text-align:center;
    padding:90px 24px;
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);
    background:
        linear-gradient(rgba(7,17,31,.72),rgba(7,17,31,.95)),
        radial-gradient(circle at center,rgba(88,214,192,.12),transparent 45%);
}

.hero-inner{
    max-width:1050px;
}

.eyebrow{
    display:inline-block;
    padding:7px 14px;
    border:1px solid rgba(88,214,192,.35);
    border-radius:999px;
    color:var(--accent);
    text-transform:uppercase;
    letter-spacing:.12em;
    font-size:.72rem;
    font-weight:800;
    margin-bottom:24px;
}

.hero h1{
    font-size:clamp(3rem,8vw,6.5rem);
    line-height:.98;
    letter-spacing:-.055em;
    margin-bottom:28px;
}

.hero h1 span{
    color:var(--accent);
}

.hero p{
    max-width:850px;
    margin:auto;
    color:var(--muted);
    font-size:1.15rem;
}

.hero-note{
    margin-top:30px;
    color:#cbd7e4;
    font-size:.95rem;
}

/* =========================
   MAIN
========================= */

.container{
    width:min(1450px,94%);
    margin:auto;
}

section{
    padding:85px 0;
}

.section-heading{
    max-width:850px;
    margin-bottom:40px;
}

.section-heading .number{
    color:var(--accent);
    font-size:.75rem;
    font-weight:800;
    letter-spacing:.15em;
    text-transform:uppercase;
}

.section-heading h2{
    font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.4rem);
    line-height:1.1;
    margin:8px 0 15px;
    letter-spacing:-.035em;
}

.section-heading p{
    color:var(--muted);
}

/* =========================
   CORE IDEA
========================= */

.principles{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);
    gap:1px;
    background:var(--line);
    border:1px solid var(--line);
}

.principle{
    background:var(--panel);
    padding:30px;
    min-height:230px;
}

.principle-number{
    font-size:2rem;
    color:var(--accent);
    font-weight:900;
    margin-bottom:15px;
}

.principle h3{
    margin-bottom:10px;
}

.principle p{
    color:var(--muted);
    font-size:.94rem;
}

/* =========================
   ENVIRONMENT AUDIT
========================= */

.audit-layout{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:1.2fr .8fr;
    gap:28px;
}

.panel{
    background:linear-gradient(145deg,var(--panel),var(--bg2));
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius:20px;
    padding:30px;
}

.panel h3{
    margin-bottom:8px;
}

.panel-intro{
    color:var(--muted);
    margin-bottom:25px;
}

.audit-item{
    padding:18px 0;
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);
}

.audit-item:last-child{
    border-bottom:none;
}

.audit-top{
    display:flex;
    justify-content:space-between;
    gap:20px;
    margin-bottom:10px;
}

.audit-top span:last-child{
    color:var(--accent);
    font-weight:800;
}

.range{
    width:100%;
    accent-color:var(--accent);
}

.score-display{
    display:flex;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    min-height:100%;
    text-align:center;
}

.score-circle{
    width:210px;
    height:210px;
    border:2px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius:50%;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    box-shadow:0 0 50px rgba(88,214,192,.08);
}

.score-circle strong{
    font-size:4rem;
    line-height:1;
}

.score-circle span{
    color:var(--muted);
    margin-top:10px;
}

/* =========================
   DEEP WORK DESIGN
========================= */

.cycle-builder{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;
    gap:28px;
}

.form-row{
    margin-bottom:20px;
}

label{
    display:block;
    color:#d8e2ec;
    font-size:.8rem;
    text-transform:uppercase;
    letter-spacing:.08em;
    font-weight:800;
    margin-bottom:8px;
}

input[type="text"],
textarea,
select{
    width:100%;
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    background:#091523;
    color:var(--text);
    border-radius:10px;
    padding:13px 15px;
    outline:none;
}

textarea{
    min-height:110px;
    resize:vertical;
}

input:focus,
textarea:focus,
select:focus{
    border-color:var(--accent);
}

.cycle-options{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);
    gap:10px;
}

.cycle-option{
    padding:16px 10px;
    background:var(--panel2);
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    color:var(--text);
    border-radius:10px;
    text-align:center;
}

.cycle-option.active{
    border-color:var(--accent);
    background:rgba(88,214,192,.1);
    color:var(--accent);
}

.primary{
    width:100%;
    margin-top:10px;
    padding:15px;
    border:0;
    border-radius:10px;
    background:var(--accent);
    color:#06120f;
    font-weight:900;
}

.primary:hover{
    filter:brightness(1.08);
}

/* =========================
   TIMER
========================= */

.timer-panel{
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    justify-content:center;
    min-height:430px;
}

.timer-status{
    color:var(--accent);
    text-transform:uppercase;
    letter-spacing:.12em;
    font-size:.72rem;
    font-weight:900;
}

.timer-task{
    font-size:1.3rem;
    margin:10px 0 20px;
}

.timer{
    font-size:clamp(4rem,10vw,7.5rem);
    font-weight:900;
    line-height:1;
    letter-spacing:-.06em;
    font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;
    margin:20px 0 30px;
}

.timer-meta{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);
    gap:10px;
    margin-bottom:20px;
}

.meta{
    padding:14px;
    background:var(--panel2);
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius:10px;
}

.meta strong{
    display:block;
    color:var(--accent);
    font-size:1.4rem;
}

.meta span{
    color:var(--muted);
    font-size:.72rem;
    text-transform:uppercase;
}

.controls{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;
    gap:10px;
}

.control{
    padding:12px;
    border-radius:9px;
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    background:transparent;
    color:var(--text);
}

.control:hover{
    border-color:var(--accent);
}

.control.primary-control{
    background:var(--accent);
    color:#06120f;
    border-color:var(--accent);
    font-weight:900;
}

/* =========================
   INTERRUPTIONS
========================= */

.interruption-grid{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);
    gap:16px;
}

.interruption{
    background:var(--panel);
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    padding:22px;
    border-radius:14px;
}

.interruption h4{
    margin-bottom:6px;
}

.interruption p{
    color:var(--muted);
    font-size:.88rem;
    margin-bottom:15px;
}

.counter{
    display:flex;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:space-between;
    border-top:1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top:15px;
}

.counter strong{
    font-size:1.5rem;
    color:var(--accent);
}

.counter button{
    width:34px;
    height:34px;
    border-radius:50%;
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    background:var(--panel2);
    color:var(--text);
}

/* =========================
   ATTENTION EQUATION
========================= */

.equation{
    margin-top:30px;
    padding:30px;
    background:#06101d;
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-left:4px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius:14px;
    overflow:auto;
}

.equation-main{
    font-size:1.5rem;
    font-weight:800;
    color:var(--accent);
    margin-bottom:12px;
}

.equation p{
    color:var(--muted);
}

/* =========================
   LESSON CARDS
========================= */

.lessons{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);
    gap:20px;
}

.lesson{
    background:var(--panel);
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    padding:28px;
    border-radius:18px;
}

.lesson-number{
    color:var(--accent);
    font-weight:900;
    font-size:.75rem;
    letter-spacing:.1em;
}

.lesson h3{
    margin:8px 0 12px;
}

.lesson p{
    color:var(--muted);
    font-size:.93rem;
}

.lesson ul{
    margin-top:15px;
    padding-left:20px;
    color:#c9d5e1;
}

.lesson li{
    margin-bottom:7px;
}

/* =========================
   REFLECTION
========================= */

.reflection{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
    gap:25px;
}

.metric-box{
    padding:25px;
    background:var(--panel);
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius:16px;
}

.metric-box h3{
    margin-bottom:10px;
}

.metric-value{
    font-size:3rem;
    color:var(--accent);
    font-weight:900;
}

.metric-box p{
    color:var(--muted);
}

.summary{
    margin-top:25px;
    padding:25px;
    background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(88,214,192,.08),rgba(143,168,255,.05));
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius:16px;
}

.summary strong{
    color:var(--accent);
}

/* =========================
   FOOTER
========================= */

footer{
    border-top:1px solid var(--line);
    padding:50px 20px;
    text-align:center;
    color:var(--muted);
}

/* =========================
   RESPONSIVE
========================= */

@media(max-width:1000px){

    .principles,
    .interruption-grid{
        grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);
    }

    .audit-layout,
    .cycle-builder,
    .reflection{
        grid-template-columns:1fr;
    }

    .lessons{
        grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);
    }
}

@media(max-width:650px){

    section{
        padding:60px 0;
    }

    .hero{
        min-height:500px;
        padding:70px 20px;
    }

    .principles,
    .interruption-grid,
    .lessons{
        grid-template-columns:1fr;
    }

    .cycle-options,
    .timer-meta,
    .controls{
        grid-template-columns:1fr;
    }

    .panel,
    .lesson{
        padding:22px;
    }
}
</style>
</head>

<body>

<!-- =========================
HERO
========================= -->

<header class="hero">

<div class="hero-inner">

<div class="eyebrow">Tech Genius • Cognitive Performance Architecture</div>

<h1>Build an environment where your <span>attention can work.</span></h1>

<p>
Deep work is not simply “trying harder.” It is the deliberate engineering
of conditions that reduce attention leakage, lower switching costs, and
allow difficult cognitive work to remain uninterrupted long enough to
produce meaningful output.
</p>

<div class="hero-note">
The objective is not to stay busy longer. The objective is to produce more
valuable work with the cognitive capacity you actually have.
</div>

</div>

</header>


<main class="container">

<!-- =========================
SECTION 1
========================= -->

<section>

<div class="section-heading">

<div class="number">01 / The Architecture</div>

<h2>Concentration is a system, not a personality trait.</h2>

<p>
When difficult work repeatedly fails, the instinct is often to blame
discipline. A better diagnosis is to inspect the environment surrounding
the behavior.
</p>

</div>

<div class="principles">

<div class="principle">
<div class="principle-number">01</div>
<h3>Reduce Switching</h3>
<p>
Every unnecessary transition asks the brain to reconstruct context.
Deep work becomes easier when the number of competing contexts falls.
</p>
</div>

<div class="principle">
<div class="principle-number">02</div>
<h3>Increase Friction for Noise</h3>
<p>
Make distracting behaviors inconvenient. Silence notifications, close
irrelevant tabs, remove visual clutter, and separate communication.
</p>
</div>

<div class="principle">
<div class="principle-number">03</div>
<h3>Protect the Start</h3>
<p>
The first minutes of a work session are expensive. Decide the objective
before the timer begins so execution does not become another planning session.
</p>
</div>

<div class="principle">
<div class="principle-number">04</div>
<h3>Recover Deliberately</h3>
<p>
Concentration is not infinite. Alternating demanding work with recovery
allows cognitive resources to be redeployed instead of continuously drained.
</p>
</div>

</div>

</section>


<!-- =========================
SECTION 2
========================= -->

<section>

<div class="section-heading">

<div class="number">02 / Environment Audit</div>

<h2>Measure the environment before blaming the brain.</h2>

<p>
Rate the conditions surrounding your next work session. The purpose is not
to produce a perfect score. It is to identify the largest source of cognitive
leakage.
</p>

</div>

<div class="audit-layout">

<div class="panel">

<h3>Attention Leakage Audit</h3>

<p class="panel-intro">
Move each slider from 0 to 10. Higher scores indicate a stronger problem.
</p>

<div class="audit-item">
<div class="audit-top">
<span>Notifications & interruptions</span>
<span id="notificationsValue">5</span>
</div>
<input class="range audit-range" type="range" min="0" max="10" value="5"
data-target="notificationsValue">
</div>

<div class="audit-item">
<div class="audit-top">
<span>Open tabs & digital clutter</span>
<span id="tabsValue">5</span>
</div>
<input class="range audit-range" type="range" min="0" max="10" value="5"
data-target="tabsValue">
</div>

<div class="audit-item">
<div class="audit-top">
<span>Task ambiguity</span>
<span id="ambiguityValue">5</span>
</div>
<input class="range audit-range" type="range" min="0" max="10" value="5"
data-target="ambiguityValue">
</div>

<div class="audit-item">
<div class="audit-top">
<span>Physical/environmental distraction</span>
<span id="physicalValue">5</span>
</div>
<input class="range audit-range" type="range" min="0" max="10" value="5"
data-target="physicalValue">
</div>

<div class="audit-item">
<div class="audit-top">
<span>Context switching</span>
<span id="switchingValue">5</span>
</div>
<input class="range audit-range" type="range" min="0" max="10" value="5"
data-target="switchingValue">
</div>

</div>

<div class="panel score-display">

<div class="score-circle">

<strong id="environmentScore">50</strong>

<span>Noise Index</span>

</div>

</div>

</div>

<div class="equation">

<div class="equation-main">
Attention Field = (Deep Minutes ÷ Total Minutes) × (1 ÷ (1 + Switches)) × 100
</div>

<p>
This model makes an important distinction: being at your desk is not the
same as being cognitively present. A two-hour work period fragmented by
constant switching can contain substantially less usable deep-work time
than a shorter uninterrupted session.
</p>

</div>

</section>


<!-- =========================
SECTION 3
========================= -->

<section>

<div class="section-heading">

<div class="number">03 / Build the Cycle</div>

<h2>Use rhythmic concentration instead of indefinite effort.</h2>

<p>
Choose a target, define the output, select a cycle, and let the environment
carry some of the discipline. Your job during the cycle is execution.
</p>

</div>

<div class="cycle-builder">

<div class="panel">

<h3>Session Architecture</h3>

<p class="panel-intro">
Design the work session before starting it.
</p>

<div class="form-row">

<label for="taskName">Primary Objective</label>

<input
type="text"
id="taskName"
placeholder="Example: Finish the homepage architecture"
/>

</div>

<div class="form-row">

<label for="definition">Definition of Done</label>

<textarea
id="definition"
placeholder="What specific evidence will prove that this session produced an output?"
></textarea>

</div>

<div class="form-row">

<label>Concentration Cycle</label>

<div class="cycle-options">

<button class="cycle-option active" data-minutes="25">
25 min
</button>

<button class="cycle-option" data-minutes="50">
50 min
</button>

<button class="cycle-option" data-minutes="90">
90 min
</button>

</div>

</div>

<button class="primary" id="startSession">
Start Deep Work Cycle
</button>

</div>


<div class="panel timer-panel">

<div class="timer-status" id="timerStatus">
Ready
</div>

<div class="timer-task" id="timerTask">
Define the work before you begin.
</div>

<div class="timer" id="timer">
25:00
</div>

<div class="timer-meta">

<div class="meta">
<strong id="cycleCount">0</strong>
<span>Cycles</span>
</div>

<div class="meta">
<strong id="deepMinutes">0</strong>
<span>Deep Minutes</span>
</div>

<div class="meta">
<strong id="switchCount">0</strong>
<span>Switches</span>
</div>

</div>

<div class="controls">

<button class="control primary-control" id="pauseButton">
Pause
</button>

<button class="control" id="finishButton">
Finish
</button>

<button class="control" id="resetButton">
Reset
</button>

</div>

</div>

</div>

</section>


<!-- =========================
SECTION 4
========================= -->

<section>

<div class="section-heading">

<div class="number">04 / Interruption Intelligence</div>

<h2>Do not merely count interruptions. Diagnose them.</h2>

<p>
An interruption is useful data. Repeated interruptions reveal where the
environment, workflow, technology, or planning system is leaking attention.
</p>

</div>

<div class="interruption-grid">

<div class="interruption">
<h4>Phone / Messages</h4>
<p>Incoming communication that breaks concentration.</p>

<div class="counter">
<strong id="phoneCount">0</strong>
<button onclick="increment('phoneCount')">+</button>
</div>
</div>

<div class="interruption">
<h4>Unplanned Research</h4>
<p>Leaving the task to investigate another question.</p>

<div class="counter">
<strong id="researchCount">0</strong>
<button onclick="increment('researchCount')">+</button>
</div>
</div>

<div class="interruption">
<h4>Task Switching</h4>
<p>Moving between projects before the current task is complete.</p>

<div class="counter">
<strong id="taskCount">0</strong>
<button onclick="increment('taskCount')">+</button>
</div>
</div>

<div class="interruption">
<h4>Environment</h4>
<p>Noise, movement, physical discomfort, or other environmental breaks.</p>

<div class="counter">
<strong id="environmentCount">0</strong>
<button onclick="increment('environmentCount')">+</button>
</div>
</div>

</div>

<div class="summary">

<strong>Strategic rule:</strong>

If the same interruption repeatedly appears, stop treating it as a
discipline problem. Treat it as a system-design problem.

</div>

</section>


<!-- =========================
SECTION 5
========================= -->

<section>

<div class="section-heading">

<div class="number">05 / Advanced Lessons</div>

<h2>The deeper intelligence behind deep work.</h2>

<p>
The timer is only the visible layer. The real advantage comes from
understanding the mechanisms underneath concentration.
</p>

</div>

<div class="lessons">

<div class="lesson">

<div class="lesson-number">LESSON 01</div>

<h3>Attention Has Switching Costs</h3>

<p>
Changing tasks is not simply changing what appears on the screen.
The brain must reconstruct the goal, relevant information, current state,
and next action.
</p>

<ul>
<li>Reduce simultaneous projects.</li>
<li>Keep relevant material visible.</li>
<li>Write down interruptions instead of acting on them.</li>
</ul>

</div>


<div class="lesson">

<div class="lesson-number">LESSON 02</div>

<h3>Ambiguity Creates Friction</h3>

<p>
A vague task such as “work on the website” creates repeated decisions.
A concrete task such as “build the responsive navigation component”
creates an executable target.
</p>

<ul>
<li>Define one output.</li>
<li>Define the stopping condition.</li>
<li>Define the next physical action.</li>
</ul>

</div>


<div class="lesson">

<div class="lesson-number">LESSON 03</div>

<h3>Friction Shapes Behavior</h3>

<p>
People tend to repeat behaviors that are easy to initiate. Engineer the
environment so desired behaviors require fewer steps than distractions.
</p>

<ul>
<li>Open the project before the session.</li>
<li>Preload necessary resources.</li>
<li>Make distracting applications harder to access.</li>
</ul>

</div>


<div class="lesson">

<div class="lesson-number">LESSON 04</div>

<h3>Recovery Is Part of Output</h3>

<p>
Trying to maximize work minutes can produce diminishing returns. High-value
performance depends on alternating demanding cognitive work with recovery.
</p>

<ul>
<li>End cycles deliberately.</li>
<li>Move away from the screen.</li>
<li>Return with a defined next step.</li>
</ul>

</div>


<div class="lesson">

<div class="lesson-number">LESSON 05</div>

<h3>Measure Output, Not Busyness</h3>

<p>
Hours are an input. Completed work is an output. A better performance
system tracks what was actually created, solved, learned, or improved.
</p>

<ul>
<li>Record completed outputs.</li>
<li>Measure deep minutes.</li>
<li>Compare output per focused hour.</li>
</ul>

</div>


<div class="lesson">

<div class="lesson-number">LESSON 06</div>

<h3>Design for Re-entry</h3>

<p>
The end of today's session determines the difficulty of tomorrow's start.
Leave a clear trail showing exactly where the work should resume.
</p>

<ul>
<li>Record the current state.</li>
<li>Write the next action.</li>
<li>Save unresolved questions separately.</li>
</ul>

